messages:
Maya C: FYI — got an escalation from a customer (internal ticket 8421). They hit a 400 on /v1/rerank and are confused about which field should contain the passages vs candidates. They sent this payload and got `unknown field 'passage'` in the response.

Maya C: Payload they sent: 
```json
{
  "query": "best onboarding snippets",
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "doc_1",
      "passage": "first para text..."
    },
    {
      "id": "doc_2",
      "passage": "second para text..."
    }
  ]
}
```

Maya C: Error: `400 Bad Request - unknown field \"passage\"` and customer also said scores came back all zeros when they tried `candidates` instead of `documents`.

Ivan P: Hmm. Two things to check — our rerank schema historically accepted `documents` (array of {id, text, ...}) and optionally `passages` nested inside each document as an array. `passage` (singular) is not a supported key. Is the customer mixing a legacy connector's format?

Nikhil R: Also confirm if they're batching queries. We recently added `queries` plural for batch rerank (array of {query, candidates}). If you send `query` as a string but wrap candidates in a nested object shape from the batch schema, validation can fail in surprising ways.

Maya C: They're not batching — single query. They tried renaming `passage` -> `text` and that got past the 400 but then scores were odd (0.0 or negative).

Ivan P: Can you paste the exact request they sent when they changed to `text`? there might be a structure vs typing issue (e.g., sending `documents` as an object instead of array).

Maya C: Sure — this is the modified payload: 
```json
{
  "query": "best onboarding snippets",
  "documents": {
    "doc_1": { "text": "first para..." },
    "doc_2": { "text": "second para..." }
  }
}
```

Maya C: Response: `200 OK` but body contains scores all 0.0 and the order is unchanged. They expected ranking.

Ivan P: Aha — that's it. If `documents` is an object map rather than an array, our server treats it as a single document with an unexpected type for candidates, then the scoring loop short-circuits and returns default scores. The validator should reject that, but we only added strict checks for the batch path recently.

Eli K: Do we have a short repro we can share with the customer (minimal valid payload and a small invalid example) so CS can send a clear explanation? Also mention limits: max 200 candidates and max 50 passages per document (these limits cause degraded results not errors if exceeded depending on config).

Ivan P: Minimal valid example for single-query rerank: 
```json
{
  "query": "best onboarding snippets",
  "documents": [
    { "id": "doc_1", "text": "first para text..." },
    { "id": "doc_2", "text": "second para text..." }
  ]
}
```

Ivan P: If you want to provide passages inside a document: 
```json
{
  "query": "best onboarding snippets",
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "doc_1",
      "text": "title or summary",
      "passages": [
        { "id": "p1", "text": "first para..." },
        { "id": "p2", "text": "second para..." }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Nikhil R: For batch rerank (multiple queries in one request) the shape is: 
```json
{
  "queries": [
    {
      "query": "q1",
      "candidates": [ { "id": "c1", "text": "..." } ]
    },
    {
      "query": "q2",
      "candidates": [ ... ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Nikhil R: Common gotcha: `queries` + `candidates` is the batch API. `query` + `documents` is the single-query API. Mixing them leads to validation acceptance but wrong runtime path.

Maya C: Perfect — I'll reply with the two examples and explain what to change. Any suggested phrasing about the 0.0 scores so it doesn't sound like a bug?

Ivan P: Say: "When the server receives an unexpected type for the candidates/documents field (e.g., an object map instead of an array), the scoring engine falls back to a default/empty scoring path which results in neutral scores. This is why you observed unchanged order and 0.0 scores. Converting to an array of documents/candidates will route the request through the normal scoring pipeline."

Eli K: Add note to docs/validate: we should add a small section under rerank input schema that explicitly enumerates: `query` vs `queries`, `documents` vs `candidates`, and the allowed nesting of `passages`. Also add examples for common mistake patterns.

Ivan P: I'll open a tiny PR to the docs and add a strict input validation check on the single-query path so the server returns 400 for a `documents` map.

infra-bot: Deploy queued: patch rerank-validator v1.2.3 -> staging (build #4217).

Nikhil R: FYI once the validator is on staging we should run the regression test with the malformed payload above to ensure it returns 400 not 200+zeros.

Maya C: Thanks — I'll hold replying to customer until we have the docs and validator change in staging, then send repro + explanation + fixed payload.

infra-bot: Deploy succeeded: patch rerank-validator v1.2.3 -> staging (build #4217).

Ivan P: Validator patch landed: returns `400` with message \"documents must be an array of objects\" for the malformed map case. PR: github.com/redwoodinc/rerank/PR/1598

Maya C: Great — closing the loop with the customer now. I'll include the minimal valid payloads and mention the batch vs single difference + limits. :thumbsup:

Maya C: (will also reference the docs PR once merged)
